{"name":"Covered Wagon","hex":"#726449","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"covered wagon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wagon with a frame (typically arched) over which a canvas cover is fixed.","A covered goods wagon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/covered_wagon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Covered wagon","blocks":[{"text":"A covered wagon, also called a prairie wagon, whitetop, or prairie schooner, is a horse-drawn or ox-drawn wagon used for passengers or freight hauling. It has a canvas, tarpaulin, or waterproof sheet which is stretched over removable wooden bows and lashed to the body of the wagon. They were a popular style of vehicle for overland migrations."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/NarrowCoveredWagon_FEP.jpg/330px-NarrowCoveredWagon_FEP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Covered_wagon"},{"title":"Covered Wagon (sculpture)","blocks":[{"text":"Covered Wagon, also known as Oregon Trail Immigrants Memorial and Pioneer Family, is an outdoor 1934 white marble sculpture by Leo Friedlander installed outside the Oregon State Capitol in Salem, Oregon, United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/BasRelief2ORCapitol.jpg/330px-BasRelief2ORCapitol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Covered_Wagon_(sculpture)"},{"title":"Wagon","blocks":[{"text":"A wagon is a heavy four-wheeled vehicle pulled by draft animals or on occasion by humans, used for transporting goods, commodities, agricultural materials, supplies and sometimes people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Wagon_Ride_P9190071.jpg/330px-Wagon_Ride_P9190071.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wagon"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://t